Subject: [PATCH] trtllm fused MoE: single-CTA post-top-K routing permutation

Unified diff against FlashInfer 0.6.18.post1
csrc/fused_moe/trtllm_backend/trtllm_fused_moe_routing_common.cu
(installed as flashinfer/data/csrc/fused_moe/trtllm_backend/...).

For precomputed top-K ids, runPostTopKPipeline launches the cluster
permutation kernel (8 CTAs x 1024 threads, cluster 8), whose cluster
barriers and DSMEM reads put a fixed latency floor on every MoE layer.
This adds a single-CTA, cluster-free permutation (int4 id loads, SMEM
histogram, block scan, parallel CTA-table fill, int4 permutation writes)
that is used for precomputed ids when numTokens >= GS2_ROUTE_MINTOK (17)
and numTokens * topK <= GS2_ROUTE_MAXN (default 16384, capped at 32768),
with 16-byte aligned ids / outputs; everything else takes the stock path.
Per-expert counts, CTA tables, padded sizes and the (expert, slot)
assignment are identical; only the within-expert row order may differ,
which the stock atomics-based kernels leave nondeterministic as well.
Runtime switches (host side): GS2_ROUTE=0 disables the new kernel,
GS2_ROUTE_LOG=1 prints the configuration once, GS2_ROUTE_AGG=1 selects
warp-aggregated histogram atomics.

Applied and built by vllm/model_executor/layers/fused_moe/
flashinfer_exact_routing.py when GS2_ROUTE is set.

